  "description": "Burrow meeting companion identities v1 (task 01a13ca2). A companion is a person's video-only second LiveKit connection, identity `video:user:<uuid>`. For each case, `person` is what the person-identity fold returns for `identity` (Elixir Meetings.person_identity/1, JS personIdentity, Swift CallParticipant) and `companion` is the companion predicate (Elixir Meetings.companion_identity?/1, JS isCompanionIdentity, Swift CallParticipant.isCompanion). The fold is a plain, case-sensitive prefix rewrite `video:user:` -> `user:`; every other string, and null, is returned unchanged. The server file is the source; client copies must be byte-identical, never edited alone.",
